Scope Resolution
cvoid main() {
    int a;          // def / local / auto / GIV  ← ①
    a = 10;         // assignment
    {
        int b;      // def / local / auto / GIV  ← ②
        b = 20;
        printf("%d", b);    // prints 22
        printf("%d", a);    // prints 10 (outer scope)
    }
    printf("%d", a);    // prints 10
    printf("%d", b);    // ← ①: b is not there → CE: undefined symbol 'b'
}

Rule: Control always searches for the nearest scope first (inner → outer → global).


